<title>USA: Jacksonville, Fla., restructured, coupon raised.</title>
<headline>Jacksonville, Fla., restructured, coupon raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co said Monday it restructured Jacksonville, Fla.'s $65.6 million bond issue, raising the coupon in 2014 to 5.50 percent from 5.125 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>CITY OF JACKSONVILLE FLORIDA</p>
<p>RE: $65,640,000</p>
<p>SALES TAX REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1996</p>
<p>(RIVER CITY RENAISSANCE PROJECT)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>NOTE COUPON CHANGE IN 2014 MATURITY.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>FGIC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 12/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT     COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>10/01/1998		1,915M    3.85  %	100.00</p>
<p>10/01/1999		1,990M    4.05  %	100.00</p>
<p>10/01/2000		2,070M    4.20  %	100.00</p>
<p>10/01/2001		2,155M    4.35  %	100.00</p>
<p>10/01/2002		2,250M    4.40  %	  4.45</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>10/01/2003		2,350M    4.50  %	  4.55</p>
<p>10/01/2004		2,455M    4.60  %	  4.65</p>
<p>10/01/2005		2,570M    4.70  %	  4.75</p>
<p>10/01/2006		2,690M    4.80  %	  4.85</p>
<p>10/01/2007		2,820M    4.90  %	  4.95</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>10/01/2008		2,955M    5.00  %	  5.10</p>
<p>10/01/2009		3,105M    5.10  %	  5.20</p>
<p>10/01/2010		3,260M    5.00  %	  5.30</p>
